","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nThe v13 source still excludes u16, its native-language unittest layer retains counts for four unsigned widths, and the original unfamiliar Agent select task has no independent proof tied to its actual generated bytes. Applicable loader, lease, cohort and deadline repairs also live on separate branches.\n\nThis candidate reconciles #816 and #817, adds bounded u16 semantics without changing existing resource type codes or limits, and validates unchanged select fragments copied from the original frozen C1 output. The language CLI now runs all eight existing native-report assertions on its own fresh report, without executing a second compiler chain. A PID/starttime-bound fixture observes descendant exit within the original total deadline.\n\n## Validation and exact identities\n\n- GitHub tree `f696b321aa98dcfa183fc72be67904b06eef0424` is identical to reviewed local commit `4078a179bd9c7f736cfb3869fdd44007be9f66e8`. Every newly uploaded blob was checked against its local Git identity.\n- The u16 branch retained 33 source/contract/reference methods, one real IPC discovery check, cold 11/11 with nested 1,215/1,215, and language 1,026/1,026 with 1,050 mathematical/reference scalar witnesses. Original 180-second qualification and three-second cleanup limits remain.\n- On frozen integrated `1be1f075`, the original C1 produced five typed subjects, with 64 whole generated-program calls, 200 projection calls and 25 SMT obligations passing. Independent fresh replay checked 555 original files and recomputed the same 25 obligations. Five types contain four distinct complete images and two distinct copied byte strings.\n- The corrected loader checker is included in that integrated proof run. Its local result is not substituted for this publication's required CI.\n- Integrated release/contract/lease/cohort/fragment controls passed 42/42. Descendant capture/deadline controls passed 49/49 after the fixture observation repair.\n- Preserve the initial 108-method integration run's one failure and one source-inode error. The latter was correctly caused by concurrent integration edits; the complete inverse method passed in an unchanged checkout. The process-state observation and its bounded correction are separately retained.\n- Final frozen-source local qualification completed on the byte-identical reviewed tree: cold 11/11 with nested 1,215/1,215 within the unchanged 180-second budget (outer command 163.924 s); language 1,026/1,026 plus all eight native-report assertions passed; the 94-method focused integration suite passed with no skips (48.747 s). These are separate, overlapping reports, not additive unique test counts. Exact-head GitHub CI remains a required gate.\n\nThe reports are overlapping qualifications with explicit source identities, not an aggregate count of independent tests. Original logs and compressed raw reports are under `review-evidence/`; `docs/HIA_V14_FOLLOWTHROUGH_20261108.md` explains the evidence boundaries.\n\n## Remaining gates\n\n**Overall HOLD; draft pending exact-head CI.** The copied-fragment proof assumes initialized normalized slots and does not prove all original surrounding contexts or the complete compiler extension. Original four-claim evaluation/adoption remains refused. Complete Core, general compiler/ABI/resources/FFI/ISA/loader correctness, complete provider interactions/billing and stable NDU economic benefit remain unestablished.\n\nThis targets the source branch. Do not retarget to metadata-only main. The public default lock and online runtime are separate operations and are not changed by this PR.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T02:47:33Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T02:53:30Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d2f7f321c88c83e67b9939b604e4b1f0fe1c0fad","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:codex